# TET PAPER II SCIENCE HANDBOOK — Cursor AI Rules
# Project: perumalrajdpr/tet-paper2-science-handbook
# Last updated: 2026-05-03

## PROJECT CONTEXT

TN-TET Paper II Science handbook project (22 chapters):
- Physics: P1-P8
- Chemistry: C1-C7
- Biology: B1-B7

Core stack:
- Python + ReportLab
- Shared layout modules in `shared/`
- Chapter modules in `chapters/`

## LAYOUT SPEC (LOCKED)

- Page size: 210mm × 290mm (custom A4 portrait)
- Margins: 20mm on all sides
- Facing pages: enabled
- Full usable width: 170mm
- Body columns: 82mm + 6mm gap + 82mm
- Theme primary color: `#0F766E`
- Preferred font: DejaVu Sans; allow safe fallback when OS font path differs

## STRUCTURE RULES

`shared/theme.py` is the source of truth for page and column constants.

Full-width blocks (must span full 170mm):
- chapter banner
- section headings
- all tables
- fact boxes (★)
- glossary container

Two-column blocks:
- regular narrative/body text between section blocks
- use `two_col_body()` or `two_col_paragraphs()` helpers

## CONTENT RULES

Always prioritize exam memorization:
- add ★ fact boxes for years, names, constants, values
- prefer dense comparison tables over long prose
- keep solved numerical problems in table form
- keep glossary in two-column format
- footer page number format must be `P1.1`, `P1.2`, `C3.1`, etc.

Never include:
- Learning Outcomes / Objectives section
- Quick Recap section

Do not add standalone "Key Facts — Rapid Revision" sections unless user explicitly asks.

## CHAPTER MODULE CONTRACT

Each chapter file should include:
1. `CHAPTER_ID`, `CHAPTER_TITLE`, `SUBTITLE`
2. `content()` returning flowables
3. `build(out_path)` used by build script
4. standalone `if __name__ == '__main__':` build block

Use `chapters/P1_measurement.py` as style reference unless user requests a different pattern.

## RENDERING SAFETY

Superscripts in table cells:
- use XML tags: `10<super>12</super>`
- avoid unicode superscripts in table cells where rendering may break

Body paragraph unicode superscripts are acceptable when font support is present.

## EXECUTION CHECKLIST

Before edits:
1. Read `shared/theme.py`
2. Read target chapter and compare with `P1_measurement.py`
3. If `shared/` changes, assume impact across all chapters

After edits:
1. Run `python build/build_chapter.py <ID>` for touched chapter
2. If shared modules changed, run broader build tests as needed
3. Fix errors before commit/push
